### Why anything was renumbered

VMID 9000 exists on both {{ cluster_seed_host }} and {{ restore_plan.source_host }}. In a
cluster a VMID must be unique across all nodes, so the seed keeps 9000 and the
other guest is renumbered. **Renumbering changes only the Proxmox identifier —
the guest's own IP address, hostname and configuration are untouched.**

